## API reference

### NavigationMenu

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:pill`, `:line` | `:pill` | Trigger style. |
| `size:` | `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg` | `:md` | Triggers, popup radius and link padding. |
| `orientation:` | `:horizontal`, `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | A bar or a sidebar (panels open beside it). |
| `icon:` | `:chevron`, `:caret`, `:plus`, `false` | `:chevron` | The indicator of every NavigationMenuIcon. |
| `morph:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Animate the popup's size and position between items. |
| `backdrop:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Dim and blur the page behind the open panel. |
| `viewport:` | `Boolean` | `true` | `false` - no popup; panels show in your NavigationMenuViewport. |
| `default_value:` | `String` | - | Open this item's panel on load (inline menus). |
| `delay:` / `close_delay:` | `Integer` | `50` | Hover open / close delays in ms. |
| `side_offset:` | `Integer` | `6` (`12` nested) | Gap between trigger and popup. |

Event: `ui--navigation-menu:change` with `{ value }` (`null` when closed).

### Parts

| Part | Props | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `NavigationMenuItem` | `value:` | Names the item (for `default_value:`). |
| `NavigationMenuTrigger` | `disabled:` | The panel opener. |
| `NavigationMenuIcon` | `icon:` | Per-trigger indicator override (`false` hides it). |
| `NavigationMenuContent` | - | The panel. |
| `NavigationMenuLink` | `href:`, `active:`, `close_on_click:`; block `{ \|link\| … }` | A link; `active` is `aria-current="page"`. |
| `NavigationMenuViewport` | - | Where an inline (`viewport: false`) menu shows its panels. |

## Accessibility

- A `<nav>` landmark - name it with `aria_label:`. Triggers are buttons with `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls`; each
  panel is a `role="group"` labelled by its trigger.
- ←/→ (↑/↓ when vertical) move between the bar's items; the arrow toward a panel opens it and focuses its first link;
  Escape closes and returns focus to the trigger; tabbing out closes it.
- The popup's enter, exit and morph transitions honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
